<title>USA: CBOT July soybeans fall on spread profit-taking.</title>
<headline>CBOT July soybeans fall on spread profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>CBOT July soybeans fell near the open after a higher start as traders took profits on the July/November spread, floor sources said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a moderate opening but we're seeing some profit-taking from those who have been long July and short November,&quot; a floor source said.</p>
<p>At 0946 CDT July soybeans were off six cents at $8.74-1/2 a bushel with November up 3-1/4 cents at $6.88.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
</text>
